source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-22
observed: Jira builds a corrupt link out of the character reference and drops the brackets, so jiro warns.
-- input.jira --
{{[x&#124;y]}}
-- rendered.html --
<p><tt><a href="#124;y" target="_blank" rel="noopener">x&amp;#124;y</a></tt></p>
-- want.md --
`[x|y]`
-- warnings.json --
[
 {
  "Line": 1,
  "Column": 1,
  "Construct": "inline-code",
  "Reason": "Jira would render a link inside this Monospace Span; inline code keeps the characters literal"
 }
]
